              <name>RPIF15</name>
              <description>configurable event input 15 rising edge Pending bit.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR1.SEC15 is disabled, RPIF15 can be accessed with non-secure and secure access.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR1.SEC15 is enabled, RPIF15 can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this RPIF15 is discarded, non-secure read returns 0.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR1.PRIV15 is disabled, RPIF15 can be accessed with unprivileged and privilege access.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR1.PRIV15 is enabled, RPIF15 can only be accessed with privilege access. Unprivileged write to this RPIF15 is discarded, unprivileged read returns 0.
When CID filtering is disabled in EXTI2_E15CIDCFGR this RPIF15 can be accessed by any processor CID.
When CID filtering is enabled in EXTI2_E15CIDCFGR this RPIF15 can only be accessed by the allowed processor CID. Dis allowed CID write to this RPIF15 is discarded and read returns 0.
This bit is set when the selected rising edge event or an EXTI2_SWIER Software trigger arrives on the configurable event line. This bit is cleared by writing a 1 into the bit.</description>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>No rising edge trigger request occurred</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>selected rising edge trigger request occurred</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
