          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>RT46</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 46.</description>
              <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT47</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 47.</description>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT48</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 48.</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT49</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 49.</description>
              <bitOffset>17</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT50</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 50.</description>
              <bitOffset>18</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT51</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 51.</description>
              <bitOffset>19</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT59</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 59.</description>
              <bitOffset>27</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT60</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 60.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT61</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 61.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR2.SEC61 is disabled, RT61 can be accessed with non-secure and secure access.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR2.SEC61 is enabled, RT61 can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this RT61 is discarded, non-secure read returns 0.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR2.PRIV61 is disabled, RT61 can be accessed with unprivileged and privilege access.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR2.PRIV61 is enabled, RT61 can only be accessed with privilege access. Unprivileged write to this RT61 is discarded, unprivileged read returns 0.
When CID filtering is disabled in EXTI2_E61CIDCFGR this RT61 can be accessed by any processor CID.
When CID filtering is enabled in EXTI2_E61CIDCFGR this RT61 can only be accessed by the allowed processor CID. Dis allowed CID write to this RT61 is discarded and read returns 0.
Note: The configurable event input is edge triggered. No glitch must be generated on this input. If a rising edge on the configurable event input occurs while writing to the register, the associated pending bit is not set.
Rising and falling edge triggers can be set for the same configurable event input. In this case, both edges generate a trigger.</description>
              <bitOffset>29</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Rising trigger disabled (for event and interrupt) for input line</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Rising trigger enabled (for event and interrupt) for input line</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>EXTI2_FTSR2</name>
