              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI49</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 49.</description>
              <bitOffset>17</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI50</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 50.</description>
              <bitOffset>18</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI51</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 51.</description>
              <bitOffset>19</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI59</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 59.</description>
              <bitOffset>27</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI60</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 60.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SWI61</name>
              <description>Software interrupt on event 61.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR2.SEC61 is disabled, SWI61 can be accessed with non-secure and secure access.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR2.SEC61 is enabled, SWI61 can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this SWI61 is discarded, non-secure read returns 0.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR2.PRIV61 is disabled, SWI61 can be accessed with unprivileged and privilege access.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR2.PRIV61 is enabled, SWI61 can only be accessed with privilege access. Unprivileged write to this SWI61 is discarded, unprivileged read returns 0.
When CID filtering is disabled in EXTI2_E61CIDCFGR this SWI61 can be accessed by any processor CID.
When CID filtering is enabled in EXTI2_E61CIDCFGR this SWI61 can only be accessed by the allowed processor CID. Dis allowed CID write to this SWI61 is discarded and read returns 0.
A software interrupt is generated independent from the setting in EXTI2_RTSR and EXTI2_FTSR. It always returns 0 when read.</description>
              <bitOffset>29</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Writing 0 has no effect.</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Writing a 1 to this bit triggers a rising edge event on event 61. This bit is auto cleared by HW.</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
