        <register>
          <name>EXTI2_RTSR3</name>
          <displayName>EXTI2_RTSR3</displayName>
          <description>EXTI2 rising trigger selection register </description>
          <addressOffset>0x40</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>RT64</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 64.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT65</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 65.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RT66</name>
              <description>Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input 66.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR3.SEC66 is disabled, RT66 can be accessed with non-secure and secure access.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR3.SEC66 is enabled, RT66 can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this RT66 is discarded, non-secure read returns 0.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR3.PRIV66 is disabled, RT66 can be accessed with unprivileged and privilege access.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR3.PRIV66 is enabled, RT66 can only be accessed with privilege access. Unprivileged write to this RT66 is discarded, unprivileged read returns 0.
When CID filtering is disabled in EXTI2_E66CIDCFGR this RT66 can be accessed by any processor CID.
When CID filtering is enabled in EXTI2_E66CIDCFGR this RT66 can only be accessed by the allowed processor CID. Illegal CID write to this RT66 is discarded and read returns 0.
Note: The configurable event input is edge triggered. No glitch must be generated on this input. If a rising edge on the configurable event input occurs while writing to the register, the associated pending bit is not set.
Rising and falling edge triggers can be set for the same configurable event input. In this case, both edges generate a trigger.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Rising trigger disabled (for event and interrupt) for input line</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Rising trigger enabled (for event and interrupt) for input line</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>EXTI2_FTSR3</name>
          <displayName>EXTI2_FTSR3</displayName>
