              <description>CPUm wakeup with interrupt mask on event input 31.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR1.SEC31 is disabled, IM31 can be accessed with non-secure and secure access.
When EXTI2_SECCFGR1.SEC31 is enabled, IM31 can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this bit is discarded, non-secure read returns 0.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR1.PRIV31 is disabled, IM31 can be accessed with privilege and unprivileged access.
When EXTI2_PRIVCFGR1.PRIV31 is enabled, IM31 can only be accessed with privilege access. Unprivileged write to this bit is discarded and read returns 0.
When CID filtering is disabled in EXTI2_E31CIDCFGR this IM31 can be accessed by any processor CID.
When CID filtering is enabled in EXTI2_E31CIDCFGR this IM31 can only be accessed by the allowed processor CID. Dis allowed CID write to this IM31 is discarded and read returns 0.</description>
